# A floor on how new a package version may be, to blunt supply-chain attacks that publish a
# malicious release and yank it minutes later.
#
# This was written as `minimum-release-age=10080`, on the belief that npm ignores keys it does
# not know. It does not: it warns on every command that the key is unknown, which turned a real
# signal into background noise. npm has no such setting, so the line enforced nothing and cost a
# warning on each install.
#
# It is kept as a comment rather than deleted so the intent survives. Enforcing it needs a tool
# that supports it (pnpm, bun) or a check of its own; neither is in place.
